# Binary assets, marked explicitly. Git guesses "binary" by looking for a NUL
# byte in the first 8KB, and a small ReportLab PDF can contain none at all — so
# it was classified as TEXT, and with core.autocrlf=true a fresh clone on Windows
# would insert a CR before every LF inside the content streams and hand you a
# corrupt file. Nothing warns you; the PDF simply stops opening.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary

# Shell scripts must keep LF endings or they break on Linux (bad interpreter ^M).
# The hardware-audit tool is copied straight to a Linux live USB and run there.
*.sh text eol=lf
# The kiosk backend carries a #!/usr/bin/env python3 shebang and is copied to the
# same Linux live USB. start-gui.sh currently invokes it as `python3 server.py`,
# so CRLF would not bite today — but the moment anything runs it directly it
# would die with the same "bad interpreter" as a CRLF shell script.
*.py text eol=lf
# Served from the station's own loopback HTTP server on Linux.
tools/gui/*.html text eol=lf
# SystemRescue autorun entry (no extension) and .desktop launcher run on Linux too.
tools/autorun text eol=lf
*.desktop text eol=lf
